# Purged from git history (2026-09-13) -- untracked working dirs kept on disk only.
anthropology/
computer-ethics/

# Default-deny for new top-level directories: a brand-new directory (a new
# corpus working dir, a scratch output dir, etc.) is ignored automatically --
# `git add -A`/`git add .` silently skips it -- unless explicitly allow-listed
# below by name. Loose top-level *files* (scripts, docs) are unaffected and
# stay addable as normal; this only catches directories. Anchored to the repo
# root (`/*/`), so it doesn't reach into already-allowed directories -- new
# files/subdirs inside tests/, sourcing/, manual_examples/ etc. are unaffected.
# Added after the anthropology/computer-ethics dirs above ended up tracked.
/*/
!/tests/
!/sourcing/
!/manual_examples/
!/example_output/
!/.github/

# Scratch working files: ad-hoc compare_two_papers.py/--out report dumps and a
# copy-paste command scratchpad. Regenerated on demand from the databases, never
# an input to anything -- keep on disk, not in git.
output.txt
match_text.txt
/notes

# Case-tracking notes that name real people in plagiarism allegations -- kept on
# disk for the reviewer, never committed.
FLAGGED_CASES_INDEX.txt
RETRACTION_WATCH_EMAIL.txt
WITHDRAWN_CASES.txt
REPORT_CLEANUP_*.txt
